IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-grounds`

-- bgg4-tests-grounds: tests for Art 95 to 98.  Expected values are written from the text
-- (quoted beside the assertion), not from the code's output.

§ `Art 95 tests`

-- "Mit der Beschwerde kann die Verletzung gerügt werden von: a. Bundesrecht; b. Völkerrecht; c. kantonalen verfassungsmässigen Rechten; d. kantonalen Bestimmungen über die politische Stimmberechtigung ...; e. interkantonalem Recht."
#ASSERT `Art 95(a) the violation of federal law can be complained of` `federal law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(a) the violation of federal law can be complained of` `international law` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(b) the violation of international law can be complained of` `international law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(b) the violation of international law can be complained of` `federal law` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(c) the violation of cantonal constitutional rights can be complained of` `cantonal constitutional rights` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(c) the violation of cantonal constitutional rights can be complained of` `another source of law` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(d) the violation of cantonal provisions on political voting rights and on popular elections and votes can be complained of` `cantonal provisions on political voting rights and on popular elections and votes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(d) the violation of cantonal provisions on political voting rights and on popular elections and votes can be complained of` `federal law` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(e) the violation of intercantonal law can be complained of` `intercantonal law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(e) the violation of intercantonal law can be complained of` `cantonal constitutional rights` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the whole Article, one assertion per limb and one outside the list
#ASSERT `Art 95 the violation of the source of law can be complained of` `federal law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95 the violation of the source of law can be complained of` `international law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95 the violation of the source of law can be complained of` `cantonal constitutional rights` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95 the violation of the source of law can be complained of` `cantonal provisions on political voting rights and on popular elections and votes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95 the violation of the source of law can be complained of` `intercantonal law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ordinary cantonal law, or any other source: the list is not closed with "nur", so not covered (fork F5)
#ASSERT `Art 95 the violation of the source of law can be complained of` `another source of law` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 96 tests`

-- (a) "ausländisches Recht sei nicht angewendet worden, wie es das schweizerische internationale Privatrecht vorschreibt"
#ASSERT `Art 96(a) the complaint that foreign law was not applied as Swiss private international law prescribes can be raised` `foreign law was not applied as Swiss private international law prescribes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(a) the complaint that foreign law was not applied as Swiss private international law prescribes can be raised` `another complaint about foreign law` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) "..., sofern der Entscheid keine vermögensrechtliche Sache betrifft": pecuniary matter no, then yes
#ASSERT `Art 96(b) the complaint that foreign law was applied wrongly can be raised` `foreign law that Swiss private international law makes applicable was applied wrongly` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(b) the complaint that foreign law was applied wrongly can be raised` `foreign law that Swiss private international law makes applicable was applied wrongly` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 96(b) the complaint that foreign law was applied wrongly can be raised` `another complaint about foreign law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the whole Article
#ASSERT `Art 96 the complaint about foreign law can be raised` `foreign law was not applied as Swiss private international law prescribes` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96 the complaint about foreign law can be raised` `foreign law that Swiss private international law makes applicable was applied wrongly` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96 the complaint about foreign law can be raised` `foreign law that Swiss private international law makes applicable was applied wrongly` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 96 the complaint about foreign law can be raised` `another complaint about foreign law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 97 tests`

-- (1) "nur gerügt werden, wenn sie offensichtlich unrichtig ist oder auf einer Rechtsverletzung im Sinne von Artikel 95 beruht und wenn die Behebung des Mangels für den Ausgang des Verfahrens entscheidend sein kann"; order: obviously wrong, rests on a violation, decisive
#ASSERT `Art 97(1) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 97(1) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 97(1) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- decisive is a second, cumulative condition ("und wenn")
#ASSERT `Art 97(1) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 97(1) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither obviously wrong nor a violation
#ASSERT `Art 97(1) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 97(1) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) military or accident insurance: "so kann jede unrichtige oder unvollständige Feststellung des rechtserheblichen Sachverhalts gerügt werden"
#ASSERT `Art 97(2) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised in military or accident insurance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 97(2) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised in military or accident insurance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 97(2) the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised in military or accident insurance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the whole Article; order: military or accident insurance, wrong or incomplete, obviously wrong, violation, decisive
-- in military insurance an ordinary wrong finding is enough, though not obviously wrong and not decisive
#ASSERT `Art 97 the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- elsewhere the same facts are not enough (paragraph 1)
#ASSERT `Art 97 the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 97 the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- military or accident insurance, finding correct and complete: paragraph 2 is silent
#ASSERT `Art 97 the complaint about the finding of the facts can be raised` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 98 tests`

-- "Mit der Beschwerde gegen Entscheide über vorsorgliche Massnahmen kann nur die Verletzung verfassungsmässiger Rechte gerügt werden."
#ASSERT `Art 98 the complaint can be raised against the decision on provisional measures` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 98 the complaint can be raised against the decision on provisional measures` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a decision on provisional measures: not covered
#ASSERT `Art 98 the complaint can be raised against the decision on provisional measures` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 98 the complaint can be raised against the decision on provisional measures` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
